# implements-port slice 3 under --walk-methods: unit_s3_arg_conv_range.lm2's exact shape, re-staged
# under its own Name so this row runs WITH the knob.  An argument's edge makes `go` throwing (its
# implicit `convert`), and a throwing method is outside the walkable subset (l2_rw_may) -- it stays
# native under the knob, exactly as a store's edge does (unit_s7_conv_range), and the root
# receives the same status 3.  `take` is walked.
fn: take (size_t: n) int
    return: 7
end: take
fn: go () int
    int: x -1
    return: take(x)
end: go
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: go(); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
